 # Working notes: 28ba67946524
+
+## Open bounded teaching finding — first-hop area, October 24
+
+Assignment `review-415d454ff10555be`; generator source remains
+`02f04089533abeaf000d8492f2b9d783cbb016e5e6553694f1ad96d3f68d62a0`, with
+canonical rule `88eede4e9a69` unchanged. This audit does not repeat the settled
+two-edge-walk defect. It checks two new executable rivals that restrict the
+first contact-graph hop to all tied largest-area or smallest-area components
+touching the blue seed, then retain only resulting shortest-distance-two targets.
+
+The lesson was fixed before evaluation: seed 17, medium, consecutive sample
+indices 0..6, with the first three as demonstrations and the next four as queries.
+No answers or rival outcomes influenced this selection. Both area rivals fit
+all three demonstrations. The smallest-first-hop rival changes query index 2
+(sample index 5, 10x19): the canonical program paints six pixels in two objects;
+the rival produces a blank grid. In the only branch demonstration, both seed
+neighbors have area four, so an area gate is invisible. In the failing query,
+the nonproductive triangle has area three and the productive bridge area four.
+The largest-first-hop rival agrees on all four queries in this bounded lesson.
+
+All 21 labels (three programs times seven inputs) were executed through the
+same-checkout protected Racket runtime. `workspace/probe_first_hop_area.py`
+reproduces the audit. The return retains `checks/28ba67946524/peer-command.json`,
+the complete original lesson, exact programs, predictions and source/runtime
+hashes in `checks/28ba67946524/first-hop-area.json`, and its one-query ambiguity
+slice in `checks/28ba67946524/ambiguity.json`. Both interpretations are retained
+as alternative-answer candidates; canonical labels remain authoritative.
+
+This finding is unresolved. A next repair should add contrasting productive
+first-hop sizes to the actual three-demo teaching context, either by constructive
+lesson selection or a motif requiring unequal-area seed neighbors. Simply adding
+the rival name to a validator would not repair the current assembly. No generator,
+reference, approval or training state changed. Evidence covers these two rivals
+and one predetermined episode, not arbitrary graph rules or a census.
 
 ## Current repair — version 3.1.0
 
