 # Working notes: 45e3c2212572
 
-Record design decisions, hypotheses, review findings, and unresolved questions here.
-Imported associated notes retain original evidence/timestamps in `evidence/associated_notes.jsonl`.
+## Current bounded review
+
+The canonical two-demonstration lesson remains ambiguous against the existing
+`vertical_rank` hypothesis: assign the top two source objects to the top output
+row, keep the original left/right orientation rule, and preserve normalized
+shape. A fresh protected-Racket replay confirms that this rule fits both public
+demonstrations but differs from the canonical query answer in 10 cells. When
+two objects are assigned the same quadrant, the executable rival uses ordered
+overwriting, matching the retained Python rival exactly.
+
+This reproduces a known limitation recorded in `evidence/associated_notes.jsonl`;
+it is not a newly discovered failure of the current generated curriculum.
+The exact original lesson, both executable programs and both query answers are
+retained privately in `workspace/evidence/vertical-rank-current.json`. This supports a
+proposed alternative-answer example without changing the normal label or
+admitting an answer stream to training.
+
+The same bounded probe checked one predeclared generated window: seed `271828`,
+medium difficulty, demonstration indices `0..3`, query indices `4..7`.
+Demonstrations 1 and 3 (zero-based) refute the rival. All eight reference outputs
+and all eight rival outputs agreed with their Python mirrors; the existing
+lesson guard passed separately for each of the four queries. No examples were
+selected by searching query answers. In total the probe performed 22 protected
+Racket evaluations across the canonical and generated lessons.
+
+Keep `EXAMPLES_NEEDED = 4` and the source-position permutation curriculum.
+This one-rival, one-window check does not establish all-seed coverage or
+universal learnability. The generator, canonical Racket, and approval state are
+unchanged; this review does not upgrade the assignment's unapproved status.
+
+Reproduce from the outer extraction:
+
+```sh
+WORK/.venv/bin/python review.py run \
+  --receipt checks/45e3c2212572/peer-command.json python3 \
+  generators/45e3c2212572/workspace/probe_vertical_rank.py \
+  --summary ../checks/45e3c2212572/peer-summary.json
+```
+
+The evidence binds the exact generator, canonical row and program, rival,
+probe, and protected runtime identity. The compact packaged receipt is
+`checks/45e3c2212572/peer-summary.json`. Imported associated notes retain their
+original evidence references and timestamps in `evidence/associated_notes.jsonl`.
